00:21:56.440 --> 00:21:58.020
My name is in those files.

00:21:58.540 --> 00:21:59.260
What do I answer?

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:02.380
It's not clear, but it has something to do with a test.

00:22:02.620 --> 00:22:05.810
I want you to find out, Mulder.

00:22:05.910 --> 00:22:08.160
I need you to do it.

00:22:08.280 --> 00:22:14.560
In a train car, buried under a quarry full of human remains.

00:22:14.620 --> 00:22:15.510
Human remains.

00:22:15.690 --> 00:22:18.050
Piled from the ground to the ceiling.

00:22:23.240 --> 00:22:29.880
Mulder, in the files I have found references to experiments carried out here in the United States.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:33.260
by scientists of the Axis who were amnestied after the war.

00:22:33.400 --> 00:22:34.800
What kind of experiment?

00:22:35.500 --> 00:22:37.500
A kind of test with human beings.

00:22:37.720 --> 00:22:39.500
These are not human beings, Scully.

00:22:39.620 --> 00:22:43.550
I would say they are extraterrestrials.

00:22:43.550 --> 00:22:45.300
Are you sure?

00:22:45.600 --> 00:22:47.230
Quite sure.

00:22:57.920 --> 00:22:59.920
Tava has vanished without leaving a trace.

00:23:00.990 --> 00:23:04.540
Nothing disappears without leaving a trace. Burn it!

00:23:04.860 --> 00:23:24.450
I've told you what I know.

00:23:24.990 --> 00:23:27.050
In my opinion, Agent Mulder is dead.

00:23:27.930 --> 00:23:29.970
Scully didn't know that Mulder escaped from the inferno.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:33.360
train fire through a tunnel abandoned by the beings who perished there

00:23:33.360 --> 00:23:37.820
located by the Navajo who submitted to an old healing ritual to make him

00:23:37.820 --> 00:23:41.480
return from the threshold of death meanwhile Scully faced a

00:23:41.480 --> 00:23:48.390
new threat they will kill her in one of these two ways that they send two men

00:23:48.390 --> 00:23:53.340
they will kill her in her house or in the garage with an unregistered weapon that they will abandon in

00:23:53.340 --> 00:23:55.500
the crime scene there were no two ways

00:23:55.500 --> 00:23:58.160
Yes, he or she.

00:23:58.760 --> 00:23:59.820
Will it be someone I know?

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:01.000
Scully, get in the car.

00:24:01.380 --> 00:24:02.300
Who do I trust?

00:24:06.980 --> 00:24:09.560
Let's shoot Scully!

00:24:09.700 --> 00:24:10.420
I won't do it.

00:24:10.520 --> 00:24:11.500
I told you to shoot her!

00:24:11.660 --> 00:24:12.040
I said no!

00:24:12.200 --> 00:24:14.780
She set me up!

00:24:15.120 --> 00:24:16.480
I just want to help her.

00:24:16.560 --> 00:24:17.920
Then pull the gun and sit down.

00:24:18.100 --> 00:24:18.760
Don't even dream about it.

00:24:18.860 --> 00:24:20.680
If you haven't come to kill me, Skinner, prove it!

00:24:20.940 --> 00:24:22.260
I haven't come to get shot either.

00:24:22.840 --> 00:24:23.900
Damn you, Skinner!

00:24:24.080 --> 00:24:25.120
Pull the gun!

00:24:25.360 --> 00:24:26.730
I told you to...

00:24:26.730 --> 00:24:26.850
Back off!

00:24:27.370 --> 00:24:29.770
What the hell is this?

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:30.500
What are you doing?

00:24:30.760 --> 00:24:31.840
Are you okay, Scully?

00:24:31.940 --> 00:24:32.380
Yes.

00:24:32.720 --> 00:24:34.570
Take the gun away.

00:24:34.590 --> 00:24:36.690
Give her the gun.

00:24:36.950 --> 00:24:39.560
Give it to her!

00:24:39.720 --> 00:24:40.650
All right.

00:24:40.950 --> 00:24:45.370
Now I want an explanation.

00:24:46.780 --> 00:24:48.500
I was warned that someone would kill me.

00:24:50.580 --> 00:24:51.600
Someone to trust.

00:24:55.700 --> 00:24:58.500
I'll put my hand in your pocket and put an end to this farce.

00:24:58.580 --> 00:24:59.240
All right?

00:25:01.310 --> 00:25:02.950
I suppose both of you know what this is.

00:25:03.030 --> 00:25:03.670
Give me the tape.

00:25:04.090 --> 00:25:04.650
I'll keep this one.

00:25:05.360 --> 00:25:06.240
Give it to me.

00:25:06.580 --> 00:25:13.720
If what you say is true, the data here is as valuable as to kill for them, and it's the only proof to take those men to justice.

00:25:14.000 --> 00:25:14.760
Do you have what I'm looking for?

00:25:15.090 --> 00:25:16.790
I've already told you, I think you know where it is.

00:25:16.930 --> 00:25:18.150
You have the damn tape!

00:25:20.460 --> 00:25:21.880
I'll know more later.

00:25:21.960 --> 00:25:23.100
I don't negotiate, he understood.

00:25:23.600 --> 00:25:26.030
Yes, sir.

00:25:26.420 --> 00:25:29.690
I don't think so. He doesn't understand anything at all.

00:25:52.940 --> 00:25:59.860
In order to kill Scully, Krychek and his accomplices killed his sister by mistake, a mistake for which Krychek would have to pay with his life.

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:22.310
I'm alive, isn't it a surprise?

00:26:22.670 --> 00:26:25.260
Yes, good, good, good. Where is it?

00:26:25.950 --> 00:26:28.550
Where you'll never find me, traitor son of a bitch.

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:30.180
Are you sure?

00:26:31.000 --> 00:26:31.820
Very sure.

00:26:31.940 --> 00:26:40.410
If I ever notice his presence nearby, I will make him a very, very famous man.

00:26:40.470 --> 00:26:45.370
Yes, thank you.

00:26:45.550 --> 00:26:46.770
I will immediately inform the group.

00:26:47.030 --> 00:26:52.640
The smoker and the man with well-kept hands who had alerted Scully,

00:26:52.790 --> 00:26:57.030
turned out to be members of a clandestine group determined to protect the secret of their work.

00:26:57.330 --> 00:26:59.620
Have you just confirmed me by phone?

00:27:00.760 --> 00:27:07.200
That a bomb has destroyed the stolen tape that contained the files and that the one who was chasing Agent Scully has died.

00:27:07.380 --> 00:27:09.160
What's wrong with Mulder and Scully?

00:27:09.380 --> 00:27:14.640
I have a meeting with the FBI. They want to make a deal.

00:27:14.880 --> 00:27:15.480
In exchange for what?

00:27:15.700 --> 00:27:19.040
For nothing. There will be no deal.

00:27:19.260 --> 00:27:25.450
I have the tape I was looking for.

00:27:27.380 --> 00:27:27.640
Really?

00:27:28.140 --> 00:27:29.910
Can I borrow it?

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:35.140
or destroy it in exchange for the security of Maldry Scully and his re-admission in the FBI.

00:27:35.380 --> 00:27:41.600
What did I tell you, Skinner? I do not negotiate, and less with scumbags who intend to throw themselves a lantern.

00:27:41.900 --> 00:27:50.060
A lantern? It has no recording, nor can it make deals, it cannot play poker if it does not have cards in

00:27:50.060 --> 00:27:59.900
hand, Mr. Skinner. Can you imagine what it must be like to die in an air accident, or from botulism, or from an attack?

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:02.120
He has a heart, nothing strange in a man of his age.

00:28:02.240 --> 00:28:03.960
Do you think I'm going crazy?

00:28:08.080 --> 00:28:09.240
I'm not done yet.

00:28:09.340 --> 00:28:09.740
Albert?

00:28:19.390 --> 00:28:24.850
I was going to beat you.

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:33.930
Now is the time to bow and kiss my ass.

00:28:34.070 --> 00:28:34.730
Listen to me!

00:28:34.730 --> 00:28:36.090
Listen to me, you son of a bitch!

00:28:36.290 --> 00:28:37.810
This man is Albert Hostin.

00:28:37.990 --> 00:28:40.810
Remember, because if something happens to Mulder and Scully,

00:28:40.870 --> 00:28:45.670
Albert will start reciting all the experiences, paragraph by paragraph, of his precious recording.

00:28:46.210 --> 00:28:47.690
Very clever, Skinner.

00:28:47.790 --> 00:28:51.940
He will be thinking that Albert is an old man and that there are many ways to kill him too.

00:28:52.280 --> 00:28:58.140
That's why, following the tradition of his town, 20 more men have memorized that information.

00:29:00.480 --> 00:29:02.680
Unless he wants to kill all the Navajos.

00:29:02.720 --> 00:29:06.630
With a simple call, everything will be known.

00:29:07.690 --> 00:29:10.870
Welcome to the wonderful world of high technology.

00:29:11.550 --> 00:29:16.750
Reunited again, Mulder and Scully followed a trail that led them to an abandoned mine in the west of Virginia,

00:29:16.990 --> 00:29:19.390
which housed a sophisticated archive system.

00:29:22.140 --> 00:29:22.980
Lots of files.

00:29:23.460 --> 00:29:26.190
Lots and lots of files.

00:29:26.550 --> 00:29:29.430
I'm looking for a minor file.

00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:30.080
What's your name?

00:29:32.300 --> 00:29:33.660
Dana Catherine Scully.

00:29:33.780 --> 00:29:38.700
It's a recent tattoo sample.

00:29:38.820 --> 00:29:41.320
I'm here, Walter.

00:29:41.620 --> 00:29:50.400
Are you aware of your sister?

00:29:50.580 --> 00:29:55.350
Yes, I know.

00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:07.670
Originally, the file was mine.

00:30:08.670 --> 00:30:09.250
I don't understand.

00:30:16.860 --> 00:30:24.630
Mulder! Mulder!

00:30:34.700 --> 00:30:34.940
Thank you.

00:31:17.880 --> 00:31:18.260
More than two.

00:31:18.320 --> 00:31:21.000
You came in a car, why didn't you call me?

00:31:21.000 --> 00:31:21.940
I wanted to see you in person.

00:31:23.240 --> 00:31:24.000
I have to ask you.

00:31:24.080 --> 00:31:27.740
I want to know something that happened a long time ago.

00:31:28.090 --> 00:31:29.840
Oh, Vox, don't...

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:32.440
I don't remember anything at all. I already told you.

00:31:32.480 --> 00:31:33.260
Mom, listen to me.

00:31:33.420 --> 00:31:34.540
When Samantha...

00:31:34.540 --> 00:31:37.480
Before she disappeared...

00:31:37.480 --> 00:31:40.320
Dad asked you if you preferred either of them.

00:31:40.600 --> 00:31:41.990
Did he ever ask you?

00:31:42.490 --> 00:31:43.290
Fox, please.

00:31:43.890 --> 00:31:45.770
Mom asked you to choose.

00:31:46.150 --> 00:31:46.630
I don't...

00:31:46.630 --> 00:31:47.490
Mom, listen to me.

00:31:47.590 --> 00:31:48.590
I need to know.

00:31:48.890 --> 00:31:51.230
Did he put you in charge of choosing?

00:31:51.630 --> 00:31:52.110
No.

00:31:52.520 --> 00:31:54.490
He couldn't choose.

00:31:54.870 --> 00:31:57.600
Your father decided.

00:31:57.960 --> 00:31:59.960
He hated him.

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:08.450
always for it and now that he is in the grave I still hate him. The medical history of

00:32:08.450 --> 00:32:12.550
Scully found in the abandoned mine was the only and mysterious clue related to his

00:32:12.550 --> 00:32:29.500
inexplicable abduction a year before. A chain or something like that. No, not today. I don't understand, I felt it under my skin.

00:32:30.350 --> 00:32:36.510
Now that I see it up close, there is a small scar on top, I can administer local anesthesia and extract it.

00:32:36.670 --> 00:32:42.650
I made a computer chip.

00:32:43.220 --> 00:32:45.240
An inexplicable event happened to him last year.

00:32:45.380 --> 00:32:49.110
It was missing for a period of time that he doesn't remember anything about.

00:32:49.340 --> 00:32:50.300
Why do you ask me?

00:32:50.420 --> 00:32:51.870
It has the mark, doesn't it?

00:32:52.070 --> 00:32:52.430
Here.

00:32:57.380 --> 00:32:59.890
In the back of the...

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:03.790
We all have it. There they put the implants.

00:33:04.170 --> 00:33:15.360
While Scully made disturbing discoveries about his abduction,

00:33:15.540 --> 00:33:19.000
Mulder chased a supposed alien on a train in motion.

00:33:19.000 --> 00:33:22.860
Both were close to unveiling the truth about alien abductions.

00:33:23.950 --> 00:33:29.180
We have discovered something, but it's not what you think.

00:33:30.250 --> 00:33:30.830
What do you know?

00:33:31.460 --> 00:33:33.080
What goes on that train is not an alien.

00:33:33.580 --> 00:33:36.660
You're wrong, Scully.

00:33:36.740 --> 00:33:38.980
Mulder, I'm inside a train wagon,

00:33:39.000 --> 00:33:41.300
identical to the one we saw in the autopsy video.

00:33:41.360 --> 00:33:43.720
And I assure you I've been here before.

00:33:44.040 --> 00:33:45.640
What are you saying, Scully?

00:33:45.920 --> 00:33:48.210
This is where they put the implant in my neck,

00:33:48.230 --> 00:33:49.230
in one of these wagons.

00:33:50.040 --> 00:33:53.000
What I mean, Mulder, is that it is not an abduction

00:33:53.000 --> 00:33:54.120
carried out by aliens.

00:33:54.560 --> 00:33:56.100
It is nothing more than a smoke curtain

00:33:56.100 --> 00:33:58.760
launched by our government to cover up a big lie.

00:33:59.080 --> 00:33:59.880
You're chasing aliens.

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:03.720
helping them to create a fiction to hide the shameful truth.

00:34:03.840 --> 00:34:05.500
And when they can't hide it, they apologize.

00:34:06.100 --> 00:34:08.020
Apologies have become part of their politics.

00:34:08.260 --> 00:34:10.220
I don't need to apologize for their lies.

00:34:10.340 --> 00:34:13.000
I don't care about the stories that have been invented to hide the crimes.

00:34:13.260 --> 00:34:15.220
I want them to pay for what has really happened.

00:34:15.500 --> 00:34:17.920
I want them to apologize for the truth.

00:34:18.320 --> 00:34:21.680
Mulder and Scully were divided on the subject of abductions.

00:34:22.040 --> 00:34:24.900
While some divers rescued from the bottom of the ocean

00:34:24.900 --> 00:34:26.800
a supposed extraterrestrial creature,

00:34:26.800 --> 00:34:29.580
thanks to the information sold by a character from the past

00:34:29.580 --> 00:34:29.900
Thank you for watching.

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:32.020
Alder and Scully, to the Scryjeck.

00:34:33.720 --> 00:34:34.080
No!

00:34:35.220 --> 00:34:36.340
On behalf of your partner.

00:34:36.960 --> 00:34:37.920
This is on my part.

00:34:40.040 --> 00:34:42.910
This is on behalf of my father.

00:34:43.090 --> 00:34:43.230
No!

00:34:43.650 --> 00:34:44.830
I didn't kill your father.

00:34:45.030 --> 00:34:46.290
And now you tell me?

00:34:46.470 --> 00:34:47.970
Why don't you go to the bathroom and wash yourself?

00:34:48.170 --> 00:34:50.630
If you don't leave in three minutes, I'll kill you and I assure you.

00:35:18.880 --> 00:35:19.280
Do you feel better?

00:35:19.400 --> 00:35:20.600
Like new.

00:35:20.900 --> 00:35:27.680
With the influence of the alien creature, Krychek returned the tape to the smoker in exchange for valuable information.

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:30.700
Where is he?

00:35:30.760 --> 00:35:32.150
I was waiting for you.

00:35:32.150 --> 00:35:34.290
Mulder, listen to me. Do you know where Krychek is?

00:35:34.450 --> 00:35:40.930
I don't know if it will make any sense to you, but he says he's heading for an abandoned missile warehouse in North Dakota.

00:35:41.090 --> 00:35:45.770
Meet me at the airport in an hour and get two tickets for the first flight to North Dakota.

00:35:46.120 --> 00:35:47.340
What's in North Dakota?

00:35:47.640 --> 00:35:49.030
The recovered UFO.

00:36:11.740 --> 00:36:13.460
He's here. He brought you, isn't he?

00:36:13.900 --> 00:36:16.370
There are only holes in the ground here, Mr. Malden.

00:36:16.450 --> 00:36:17.730
And why are these men here?

00:36:17.790 --> 00:36:19.110
I don't have to answer you.

00:36:19.170 --> 00:36:21.190
The UFO is here. It's what Krychek is looking for, isn't it?

00:36:21.670 --> 00:36:24.410
Krychek? Alex Krychek disappeared five months ago.

00:36:25.190 --> 00:36:26.390
We've seen the corpses.

00:36:26.790 --> 00:36:27.610
They haven't seen anything.

00:36:27.910 --> 00:36:28.870
He won't get away with it!

00:36:30.730 --> 00:36:31.730
He will not bury the truth!

00:36:32.010 --> 00:36:42.120
This year, the investigations of Mulder and Scully around terrifying and strange phenomena will continue.

00:36:42.460 --> 00:36:49.780
While Scully follows his investigations from a scientific perspective,

00:36:49.860 --> 00:36:55.840
Mulder has found evidence that makes him think that in the X Experiences there are secrets until now unsolved.

00:37:05.850 --> 00:37:06.490
My patience is running out!

00:37:32.080 --> 00:37:34.340
The murderer will continue to kill until he is stopped.

00:37:34.520 --> 00:37:35.780
Can you see him physically?

00:37:36.960 --> 00:37:40.650
No, but I know more about his personality.

00:37:40.930 --> 00:37:43.700
He thinks he's divine.

00:37:44.080 --> 00:37:45.120
Is he?

00:37:45.440 --> 00:37:46.680
I hope not.

00:37:46.860 --> 00:37:49.620
I see things that he has seen.

00:37:49.820 --> 00:37:50.500
And what has he seen?

00:37:52.860 --> 00:37:53.140
You.

00:37:58.840 --> 00:37:59.040
Stop him.

00:38:01.180 --> 00:38:02.180
Where are we?

00:38:02.300 --> 00:38:04.760
In a kitchen.

00:38:05.650 --> 00:38:07.130
You are looking for someone.

00:38:07.700 --> 00:38:09.940
He is behind you, but you don't know.

00:38:10.220 --> 00:38:12.670
You come close, stealthily, and...

00:38:12.670 --> 00:38:13.510
God.

00:38:14.190 --> 00:38:15.600
What? What have you seen?

00:38:16.150 --> 00:38:18.360
He has a knife stained with blood.

00:38:18.580 --> 00:38:19.760
Five men will die.

00:38:20.120 --> 00:38:21.240
It's over.

00:38:21.460 --> 00:38:22.420
Five men will die!

00:38:23.330 --> 00:38:24.490
That will be my justice.

00:38:25.200 --> 00:38:26.580
That will be my law.

00:38:26.800 --> 00:38:28.780
No one will free himself from that death penalty.

00:38:30.090 --> 00:38:37.210
It will be a crime, because there will be no witnesses, no evidence to present, no lawyers to comply with their duty.

00:38:37.390 --> 00:38:39.970
Those men will receive a...

00:38:39.970 --> 00:38:40.720
...final death!

00:38:50.010 --> 00:38:50.930
Nietzsche has returned.

00:38:51.580 --> 00:38:54.810
Reincarnated? He would define it as a transmigration of the soul.

00:39:31.790 --> 00:39:35.250
What reason could the murderer have to extract the victim's adipose tissue?

00:39:35.930 --> 00:39:38.220
What kind of person are we looking for?

00:39:38.380 --> 00:39:39.470
I don't know.

00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:04.760
When I got here, I started to wonder if what Lieutenant Colonel Stans had described could be a case of astral projection.

00:40:04.760 --> 00:40:09.220
Do you insinuate that that rag man abandons his body and flies around the city killing people?

00:40:09.580 --> 00:40:14.500
Those who practice astral projection say that by auto-hypnosis the astral body can separate and go anywhere.

00:40:14.860 --> 00:40:17.900
Sometimes it is invisible, but sometimes it is shown as an apparition.

00:40:17.960 --> 00:40:22.340
They also say that the astral body has a much greater psychokinetic capacity than the physical body.

00:40:31.210 --> 00:40:31.730
What are you suggesting?

00:40:32.740 --> 00:40:35.920
The murderous snails were an experiment that went wrong

00:40:35.920 --> 00:40:38.620
and they were released without warning the population.

00:40:38.920 --> 00:40:43.600
Who knows if the government has created a new kind of murderous cockroaches.

00:40:44.260 --> 00:40:44.740
God!

00:40:47.050 --> 00:40:48.410
Dud, what's wrong with you, man?

00:40:53.300 --> 00:40:57.480
I'm getting goosebumps!

00:40:57.700 --> 00:40:58.520
What's wrong?

00:41:01.270 --> 00:41:01.750
Cucarachas!

00:41:01.750 --> 00:41:02.050
What?

00:41:03.010 --> 00:41:03.490
Cucarachas!

00:41:03.690 --> 00:41:04.170
Everywhere!

00:41:08.480 --> 00:41:09.910
They have me surrounded!

00:41:10.860 --> 00:41:12.660
Mulder, you have to get out of there right now!

00:41:13.000 --> 00:41:14.380
Police! To the ground!

00:41:14.730 --> 00:41:15.170
Okay!

00:41:15.310 --> 00:41:15.830
To the ground!

00:41:16.070 --> 00:41:17.670
Okay, okay...

00:41:18.050 --> 00:41:20.250
Calm down, calm down...

00:41:20.250 --> 00:41:27.830
Let me see his face, I thought...

00:41:32.010 --> 00:41:59.340
That's it, that's it, hey Collins, listen, please, please, let go of that

00:42:00.920 --> 00:42:05.600
Model hypnotized the judge, he ate the coconut.

